  "structure": {
    "block_count": 58,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "How to Take Professional-Looking Newborn Photos at Home",
        "text_sha256": "6479a68563ff19bc12250d4fdb7b02130bd12f3c0d78b938b82addc7624468d2",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "baby photoshoot at home",
        "text_sha256": "7865010e271e4992bb786b08c6bc7d59f0bf63b0a0a920618d669fecfc4ff175",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Capture your baby's first weeks — without shelling out for a pro photographer — using these tips from parents who went the DIY route.",
        "text_sha256": "a4373999a4bb1b4ab2e33121588bb0a5f426ae8e4b821111570b245f33ba3737",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Those first few days with your baby are so special. You're going to want to capture those tiny fingers, round cheeks and adorable newborn faces forever, but professional photo shoots can cost hundreds of dollars.",
        "text_sha256": "ee5d5da48d9b1814d9b2e3170bf1e1b01aefd4ba1f7fb966009fc9386c5d0a68",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If paying for a photographer isn't in your budget, you can still capture beautiful photos of your baby's first days. Parents in the What to Expect community got to talking about how they DIYed their newborn pictures. Here are the tips that got them through their photo shoots.",
        "text_sha256": "a71825f37eef3220a34e2b97e90b9b5d3d15f79051a2d3510619a16f91c8b0c1",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Take the photos early",
        "text_sha256": "0993b2ed790c63db0e69543aa8e91b5b49ebb9846d66fd767de08da08047eefb",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Those first days whiz by, but making some time for photos will help you preserve those special moments forever.",
        "text_sha256": "bd00ed3d9c8f9055c2b489e10fbd5224631ec7c9d354f31064141d27f6cb7847",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"The ideal time is when baby is five to 10 days old so they are still sleepy and you can easily pose them.\" — missthompson",
        "text_sha256": "5c86ab4708e2488b836963b7805820fbb9b07c2ad8e7b00ef8922dd42f0e2a5b",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Get baby ready",
        "text_sha256": "c5205d875837e9e51fdc2e19753cf78181e3bd5cc8a7da766e5f754fdc462de3",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Take cues from the star of the show when planning the shoot.",
        "text_sha256": "08f5af6b288ef1c9d38ddc4f104d5b5405b0975a2cc8193f18a41d5c1b5cac2e",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I just made sure she was well fed, sleepy and warm. I also used a white noise machine to make sure the sound of the camera didn’t startle her. I did it in the morning when she’s usually the sleepiest and the light is best.\" — tilly_mae",
        "text_sha256": "d59f772e7ada7a05c3cad6e65d6629ff81a8426771ade6aac117a27f84be7734",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Filter the light",
        "text_sha256": "4fb30025709c0eb4275f42873733f20ec5c5fadd5bc8649e1f7289af72b1f393",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Letting in a lot of light can greatly improve your pics, but so can filtering it with sheer curtains or a sheet.",
        "text_sha256": "a41086a74a8f62bf24e4c4af685ab5a18a0dd93823473528b169aee0ddfd24c7",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I found the room in my house with the best natural light and put a white sheet up so that the light wasn't so harsh and it filtered through nicely.\" — tilly_mae",
        "text_sha256": "833d456558dfb87af01533c67b8f92d0f7e5c65fa349a40ac46cc8107a2e52c5",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Create a cute background",
        "text_sha256": "df815286ff5424d7d15f7befb0c184d993c86b520f59aa1bfe5481bc82819661",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Switch up the theme by using different patterned blankets as backdrops and swapping in props like stuffed toys. Tip: A from-above shot is easy to get and your baby can stay on her back.",
        "text_sha256": "3b5fb4e6f82856521247e234873cc2a366dba158ec0c451c96746d4050759c16",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Just used bed sheets on our living room couch when he was tiny with blankets and pillows underneath to help with propping him up.\" — jessieg123",
        "text_sha256": "aae103a939a9e48b99b9dd0373b21881608b64a3d39bd35942879f76c057eecd",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Use a pillow",
        "text_sha256": "86c03f5ebf83386f5104740615d7bcd235b7a57ac5841e88f0ba0242183387aa",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While it’s okay to pose your baby with pillows and blankets for a short photo shoot, don't leave her unattended, especially when she’s sleeping. As soon as you’re finished, make sure you transfer her to a safe sleeping position .",
        "text_sha256": "e47ae49011ce2df94a0c40d992bdc170ddd816bc0c85fffc2a912640df959933",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Use a Boppy or some sort of pillow to prop up your baby, use a blanket as the backdrop and make sure the back of it is held tight to get that infinite look.\" — leguene",
        "text_sha256": "545657dc2694f250530f0ce3695574c90af5c9f7d8d1a5366c485bd42dc83b2f",
        "word_count": 36
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Pick up your iPhone",
        "text_sha256": "250f98190d1281cc6528b1d23d2d0778d24000848b38b32150e522933e270874",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You don’t need a professional camera to capture professional-looking shots. A smartphone camera can yield surprisingly crisp results. Bonus tip: Use portrait mode!",
        "text_sha256": "dab67773e8b9efe8b3f4e7918d172716a40d54a8c30fcd5824e06aa0c61b0674",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"We actually tried taking our photos with our Canon Rebel, but they weren't turning out so I switched to my iPhone and they looked so much better!\" — Littleashley",
        "text_sha256": "11034b65362f95fc0d3e960ce4734bc68724e75214804fd353cdb435589664fd",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Do a costume change",
        "text_sha256": "f1f2db5e5b15e45360280769707db0d69760ba84ac7eea9b09b6f97d372089dd",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have a few accessories or different clothes at the ready for your miniature model to change into. You’ll end up with a bunch more options.",
        "text_sha256": "8de45b133d2aca314ba6938b69e7c6eed157e65316c461d14d8fdb37fafc04fd",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"You can change headbands or outfits to get more variety in your photos.\" — aleashya",
        "text_sha256": "46263ca511ad8f53573093d9a0698ec9b59b542aaa6f2e2e4e152205e4ed2401",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Get close",
        "text_sha256": "2cf3e3b1779a774c2b89d805df3005739f81f16b5276d400d4f6cae5aac073c1",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Try to capture the details, like the tiny yawns, smiles, fingers and toes. Focusing on these details will remind you how delicate your baby once was and also might help you capture some sweet moments.",
        "text_sha256": "20f89267c2c09c5e8a6a055019ce63f83a6ad0a2880a9d0908712fa566d56fb1",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Try a different angle",
        "text_sha256": "e11bf8b50885bf31e954c6f0f08ccf0e3ea164987de9066694cba551e5c9f1b5",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Get creative with your stance while photographing your little peanut .",
        "text_sha256": "57d0b02911e5d0342108cb65318a4ae1e31e4f57145146fa19561931fe31131f",
        "word_count": 11
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Take the photos from at least three different angles. That will also give you more of a variety to choose from. However, when taking the photo, do not shoot upward towards the baby. What I mean by this is not to shoot the photo where you can see up the baby's nose.\" — aleashya",
        "text_sha256": "10f2af4851f3215f0e4328f32595962f91e6140c7a978cda1d4da51ffc79a1b0",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Be patient",
        "text_sha256": "17fe179f374c96e68928d3aaf0707803db7f2a7c676dbf7a0e62c44f3f263de2",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A little preparation goes a long way, but be prepared to go with the flow once the photo shoot starts.",
        "text_sha256": "b737c0b8351deedddee69bb1e4254572fe9d12afc668a296432d244282712453",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Have everything set up before you even pick up the baby, and make sure you take some practice shots first. (You can even use a doll to practice and see what it will look like) ... Then, once you do place her, have lots of patience, and be ready to stop and do it over in a while if she gets frustrated. Usually, I resigned myself to the fact that I won't get the exact photo I want, but it will be good enough.\" — danielmeowmeow",
        "text_sha256": "236e7db74f9394cb3a81ad43e5c7a5d2a28142092779c59a5345a3b6c2a7f5cc",
        "word_count": 86
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Edit your photos",
        "text_sha256": "dfddada445485ea096d517472cff605a578f3f552ecfdb4b6741e2acfd3d2db6",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Don't be afraid to desaturate, go black and white, add a filter and play around with color. It can give a simple photo a totally new look. Experiment with the different Instagram features, the Photoshop Express Photo Editor app or any other photo editing app you like.",
        "text_sha256": "46f1ff46f5051325602c0452df495b04e8fc3dfa1cd1bf8192e3ae364d867beb",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Go easy on yourself",
        "text_sha256": "7ab1ecef4b30944bdd4f5c2aeb2ad9303662fcf7f6613b86891984f24e532976",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You can take beautiful photos as an amateur, but the final results might not look exactly like what the pros do, and that’s okay.",
        "text_sha256": "b37bf54bc3d3fa4467df11e8bc035b596eb59d5f759d96419a9b94b1b0c46687",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Keep it simple. Pinterest can be great for ideas, but keep in mind a lot of those photos are composites, you can't copy them without serious editing.\" — NicoleMoses613",
        "text_sha256": "7778e6830519d018634bca978777b1a667909fcd30907e1d5eefcbfe402f9129",
